What is Wire Electrical Discharge Machining (WEDM)?
Wire Electrical Discharge Machining (WEDM) is a non-traditional machining process that uses electrical discharges (sparks) to cut conductive materials with high precision. The process utilizes a continuously moving thin wire electrode that erodes material from the workpiece submerged in dielectric fluid, enabling the production of complex geometries with tight tolerances and excellent surface finishes.

WEDM technology has become indispensable for industries requiring micron-level accuracy, especially where conventional machining methods struggle with hard materials or intricate designs. The process offers distinct advantages including minimal mechanical stress on workpieces, the ability to machine hardened materials, and superior edge quality compared to conventional cutting methods.

